# Root /tests/ — IGNORED BY DEFAULT, published only by explicit exception.
#
# Lives at repo root /tests/ so future test files (frontend, integration,
# end-to-end) can sit alongside the sidecar-focused ones. The pnpm test:*
# scripts in /package.json reference these files. See the
# polished-questing-beacon plan notes for the original rationale.
#
# WHY `/tests/*` AND NOT `/tests/`: git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so `/tests/` followed by `!/tests/foo.ts` leaves foo.ts ignored —
# the negation silently does nothing, and you cannot tell that from reading it.
# Excluding the directory's CONTENTS instead keeps exactly the same
# fail-closed default while making per-file re-inclusion actually work.
# Same reason each subdirectory below is re-included and then re-emptied:
# without the `/tests/<dir>/*` line the whole subdirectory comes back.
#
# THE POLICY IS FAIL-CLOSED. A file dropped into tests/ tomorrow is IGNORED
# until someone writes a `!` line for it here. Publication is never the
# default; it is always a deliberate, reviewed, per-file act.
#
# Adding a `!` line is NOT sufficient on its own. Every path negated below
# must also appear in scripts/tests-allowlist.txt, and
# scripts/check-tests-allowlist.sh fails the build if anything tracked or
# merely VISIBLE under tests/ is missing from that list. The two lists are
# deliberately independent: a hurried `!` here must fail a check, not redefine
# what the check expects.
#
# NEVER NEGATE, under any deadline:
#   tests/route-b-*.json  — a REAL CORTEX EXPORT (108 real skill names, real
#     sourceIds, 12 real engram names). `route-b-fixture.clean.json` is
#     MIS-NAMED: only personal-name strings were stripped. It is not clean.
#   tests/corpus-routing-experiment.ts, tests/infer-crosscheck.ts,
#   tests/savings-experiment.ts  — same real-cortex corpora.
#   tests/rag-comparison-study/  — a local research study comparing Graphnosis
#     to Airweave (paper) and a Milvus-Groq RAG stack. See the
#     peaceful-booping-gosling plan notes. Never ships.
#   tests/desktop/*.test.ts — class (b)/(c): working reproductions of defects
#     live on the shipped build. Only the harness files are published.
#
# The publishable set below is the class (a) set from the 2.59a disclosure
# classification — defect fixed AND adopted by every shipped consumer.
/tests/*

# harness / fixtures
!/tests/run-all.ts
!/tests/_helpers.ts
!/tests/_fixtures.ts
!/tests/fixtures/
/tests/fixtures/*
!/tests/fixtures/skill-walk-golden.json

