# Denylist of real names/orgs that scripts/pre-commit-guard.sh refuses to let
# into a commit. The list is itself the sensitive data — publishing a curated
# set of "strings this project considers sensitive" discloses those strings.
# Stays local; the tracked .example holds synthetic entries documenting the
# format. The guard fails CLOSED (exit 1) when this file is missing or empty.
scripts/.sensitive-needles
!scripts/.sensitive-needles.example

# ── apps/desktop-sidecar/tests/ — IGNORED BY DEFAULT, published by exception ──
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: this directory had no ignore stack at all, unlike root
# /tests/. 36 files here are classified (b)/(c) by scripts/disclosure-held.txt
# — runnable reproductions of defects that are live on the shipped build — and
# a single `git add apps/desktop-sidecar/tests/` published every one of them.
# The release has to stage inside this exact directory, so the trap was armed.
#
# Same shape as /tests/* above, and for the same reason: git does not descend
# into an excluded DIRECTORY, so `dir/` followed by `!dir/foo` leaves foo
# ignored. Exclude the CONTENTS with /*, then negate each publishable path.
#
# FAIL-CLOSED: a file dropped in here tomorrow is IGNORED until someone adds
# an explicit negation. scripts/check-disclosure-tags.sh fails when anything
# tagged (b)/(c) is NOT ignored.
/apps/desktop-sidecar/tests/*

# publishable suites — verified 2026-08-03 to be exactly the set already tracked,
